IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lt-common`
IMPORT `lta-core`
IMPORT `rcr-core`
IMPORT `lta-seat`

-- Cases for lta-seat.l4: the owner's questions, asked with plain answers.
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited texts (the arithmetic checked in the independent
-- calculator, scratchpad au-tas-4/hand.py); no value was copied from the encoding's output. Several cases ask the same
-- facts as lta-cases-core.l4 and rcr-cases-core.l4 and must give the same answers. The Hobart CPI figures are
-- ILLUSTRATIVE (137.1, 139.3, 142.0, 145.5 for March 2024 to March 2027).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the owner's questions`

`illustrative Hobart CPI` MEANS LIST 137.1, 139.3, 142.0, 145.5

§§ `Land tax -- who pays, and when`

-- Settled on 30 June 2026: liable for 2026-27. Settled on 1 July 2026: not (finding 10).
#ASSERT `Am I the owner liable for land tax on this land this year` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I the owner liable for land tax on this land this year` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1))
-- Sold, settled 1 July 2026: the seller is still liable for 2026-27; settled 15 June 2026: not.
#ASSERT `Am I the owner liable for land tax on this land this year` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2005 1 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I the owner liable for land tax on this land this year` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2005 1 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 15))
-- s 3A(2): the life tenant, not the owner in remainder.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I the owner liable for land tax on this land this year` 2026 TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2005 1 10) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 10))
#ASSERT `Am I the owner liable for land tax on this land this year` 2026 FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2005 1 10) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 10)

#ASSERT `Can I be made to pay all the land tax on land I own with others` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be made to pay all the land tax on land I own with others` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my jointly owned land assessed apart from my own land`

#ASSERT `On what day is my land tax due` (YMD 2026 9 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 20
#ASSERT `On what day is my land tax due` (YMD 2026 9 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 8 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 15

#ASSERT NOT (`Can I pay my land tax in instalments` 500)
#ASSERT `Can I pay my land tax in instalments` 500.10

§§ `Land tax -- classes`

#ASSERT `What share of the land do I own for land tax` 100 1 0 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `What share of the land do I own for land tax` 100 3 0 EQUALS 100 DIVIDED BY 3
#ASSERT `What share of the land do I own for land tax` 70 2 30 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `Do I own at least half of the land for land tax` 100 2 0
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I own at least half of the land for land tax` 100 3 0)
#ASSERT `Do I own at least half of the land for land tax` 70 2 30
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I own at least half of the land for land tax` 70 2 0)

#ASSERT `Is my home principal residence land this year` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my home principal residence land this year` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my home principal residence land this year` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my home principal residence land this year` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Is the block next to my home principal residence land` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the block next to my home principal residence land` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Is the late owner's home still principal residence land this year` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the late owner's home still principal residence land this year` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

#ASSERT `Can my land's classification be kept after a disaster` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: for up to this many years, if the Commissioner is satisfied of these facts; meanwhile no other land of yours can be principal residence land` 2
#ASSERT `Can my land's classification be kept after a disaster` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no extension under s 37B`

#ASSERT `Is my land primary production land` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my land primary production land` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my land primary production land` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `Is my business at home a qualifying home business` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 50
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my business at home a qualifying home business` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 60)

§§ `Land tax -- the pensioner exemption`

-- The share facts are asked plainly and counted by the core's 50% test (finding 26). Two joint tenants of the whole:
-- 50% each, exempt. Three: a third each, not.
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 100 2 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 100 3 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` FALSE 100 1 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 100 1 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 100 1 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 100 1 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- A couple holding 70% as joint tenants, Housing Australia 30% under Help to Buy: 35 / 70 = 50% each (s 11A, finding 4).
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 70 2 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The same 35% each with no Help to Buy share left out: not 50%.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 70 2 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A tenant in common holding 60% alone: exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my land exempt because I hold a pensioner card` TRUE 60 1 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `Land tax -- how much`

-- Home $400 000 (lived in, no other use), shack $200 000, rental $300 000: $500 000 of general land, $1 737.50.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 300000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1737.50
-- The home with a 70 m2 shop (land 600 m2, upper floor 100 m2) and the rental: $40 000 + $300 000, $1 017.50.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 70 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 300000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1017.50
-- The same with a Pensioner Concession Card: the whole home is exempt, $837.50 (finding 1).
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 70 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 300000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 837.50
-- The shop is a qualifying home business: no apportionment, $837.50 on the rental.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 70 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 300000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 837.50
-- A home alone: nil.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
-- The owner has moved to a retirement village and no related person lives in the home: general land, $1 287.50.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE TRUE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1287.50
-- Three siblings, joint tenants, who all live there: none owns half, so general land, $1 287.50 (finding 3).
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 FALSE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1287.50
-- A $500 000 home, 300 m2 of its 1 000 m2 used otherwise: $150 000 general, $162.50; nil with a TPI special rate pension.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 500000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 0 300 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 162.50
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 500000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 0 300 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
-- A special rate pensioner not totally and permanently incapacitated: no exemption, $162.50.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 500000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 0 300 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 162.50
-- 2025-26: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2025 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 300000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the financial year begins before 1 July 2026: sections 13 and 37 of the Land Tax Act were amended from that day (No. 19 of 2026) and the earlier wording is not in the deposited consolidation`

-- Cases the encoding does not cover (finding 24). A foreign owner (acquired after 1 July 2022) with a $300 000 rental:
-- foreign investor land tax may be payable on it, so not covered.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 300000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `an owner of this general land may be a foreign person liable to foreign investor land tax (Land Tax Act Division 1A; Land Tax Rating Act s 6A: 2% of the assessed land value, on top of the Schedule 1 amount), which is not encoded`
-- The same owner with only the home, lived in and used for nothing else: no general land, so s 16C cannot apply; nil.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
-- The home with the 70 m2 shop and nothing else: $40 000 apportioned as general land (s 16A(2)(a)), so not covered,
-- although Schedule 1 alone would charge nil.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 70 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `an owner of this general land may be a foreign person liable to foreign investor land tax (Land Tax Act Division 1A; Land Tax Rating Act s 6A: 2% of the assessed land value, on top of the Schedule 1 amount), which is not encoded`
-- A conservation covenant on the shack (s 19A): not covered.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2026 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 200000 300000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `some of the land is exempt, wholly or partly, on a ground other than s 19(a)-(b) (ss 19(ba)-(e), 19A-19E, 29, 30A), and those exemptions are not encoded`
-- A foreign owner in 2025-26: the year is outside the deposit first.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I pay this year` 2025 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 300000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the financial year begins before 1 July 2026: sections 13 and 37 of the Land Tax Act were amended from that day (No. 19 of 2026) and the earlier wording is not in the deposited consolidation`

#ASSERT `How much land tax is charged on this value of general land` 2026 600000 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 3237.50
#ASSERT `How much land tax is charged on this value of general land` 2026 124999 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `How much land tax is charged on this value of general land` 2026 125100 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 50.40
#ASSERT `How much land tax is charged on this value of general land` 2027 450000 EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 1512.50

§§ `Land tax -- rebates`

-- A vacant block at $200 000 ($387.50 of land tax) on which a home was built and moved into during 2026-27.
#ASSERT `Can I get a land tax rebate for building a home` 2026 TRUE TRUE FALSE 387.50 EQUALS `yes: a rebate, in dollars, of` 387.50
-- The builder still owned the old home during the year: no s 37 rebate (finding 13).
#ASSERT `Can I get a land tax rebate for building a home` 2026 TRUE TRUE TRUE 387.50 EQUALS `no rebate under this section`
#ASSERT `Can I get a land tax rebate for building a home` 2025 TRUE TRUE FALSE 387.50 EQUALS `not covered here` `the financial year begins before 1 July 2026: sections 13 and 37 of the Land Tax Act were amended from that day (No. 19 of 2026) and the earlier wording is not in the deposited consolidation`
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for the building rebate` EQUALS `the Land Tax Act sets no time limit for applying`

-- New home bought 15 May 2026 at a land value of $450 000 ($1 512.50 for 2026-27), old home sold by a contract of
-- 10 September 2026, possession in October 2026, no rent: the rebate is the $1 512.50.
#ASSERT `Can I get a land tax rebate for moving between two homes` 2026 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2012 2 1) (YMD 2026 5 15) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE 1512.50 EQUALS `yes: a rebate, in dollars, of` 1512.50
-- Neither home bought in the 3 months before 1 July: no rebate (finding 19).
#ASSERT `Can I get a land tax rebate for moving between two homes` 2026 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2012 2 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE 1512.50 EQUALS `no rebate under this section`
-- The old home acquired in the 3 months instead (bought in May 2026 and moved into; the other home is the one left):
-- either home will do (finding 19).
#ASSERT `Can I get a land tax rebate for moving between two homes` 2026 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 2) (YMD 2015 8 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 900 EQUALS `yes: a rebate, in dollars, of` 900
-- Sale contract signed on 1 October 2026: too late.
#ASSERT `Can I get a land tax rebate for moving between two homes` 2026 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2012 2 1) (YMD 2026 5 15) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 1512.50 EQUALS `no rebate under this section`
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply for the moving rebate` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2027 9 30

§§ `Land tax -- telling the Commissioner`

#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner about a change in my land` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: notify the Commissioner in writing within this many days, or face a fine of up to this many penalty units` 30 10
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Commissioner about a change in my land` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no notice is required of me`
-- s 11(5)-(6): served with the Commissioner's notice, a statutory declaration within 14 days (finding 25).
#ASSERT `Must I state my interest in the land to the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS `yes: state your interest in the land by statutory declaration, lodged with the Commissioner within this many days after the notice was served on you` 14
#ASSERT `Must I state my interest in the land to the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS `no statement is required of me`

§§ `Council rates -- eligibility and applying`

#ASSERT `Am I an eligible pensioner for the rates remission` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible pensioner for the rates remission` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I an eligible pensioner for the rates remission` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT `By what day must I apply for the rates remission` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 30

-- Pensioner Concession Card, living at home, applies on 10 August 2026: granted.
#ASSERT `Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0
-- The same, applying on 31 March 2027: too late in 2026-27 (finding 14).
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2027 3 31) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)
-- No card on 1 July 2026: not granted for 2026-27.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2026 8 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)
-- Single, in residential aged care, no rent, statutory declaration given: granted in the first and second year, not
-- the third (s 4(3C), finding 17).
#ASSERT `Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0
#ASSERT `Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 2)
-- Married, in aged care, spouse at home: granted, and s 4(3C) does not limit it.
#ASSERT `Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2026 8 10) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5
-- A tenant who pays no rates cannot apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my council grant my rates remission application` (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)

§§ `Council rates -- how much`

#ASSERT `What is the most my council can remit this year` 2026 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 393
#ASSERT `What is the most my council can remit this year` 2025 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 386
#ASSERT `What is the most my council can remit this year` 2024 FALSE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 558.50
-- 2024-25 needs no CPI figure (finding 23).
#ASSERT `What is the most my council can remit this year` 2024 TRUE EMPTY EQUALS `the amount, in dollars, is` 379.41
#ASSERT `What is the most my council can remit this year` 2028 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `not covered` `a Hobart CPI figure that the year's maximum remission needs was not given`

-- Applied 10 August 2026, eligible throughout. 2026-27: 30% of $1 800 = $540, capped at $393.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2026 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1800 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the remission, in dollars, is` 393
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2026 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the remission, in dollars, is` 300
-- Not a water and sewerage customer: cap $578; 30% of $1 800 = $540.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2026 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1800 FALSE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the remission, in dollars, is` 540
-- 2025-26, the year before the application (s 4(1D)): 30% of $1 700 = $510, capped at $386.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2025 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1700 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the remission, in dollars, is` 386
-- Not eligible on 1 July 2025: nothing for 2025-26.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2025 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1700 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `no remission for this year`
-- 2024-25, two years back: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2024 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1700 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `no remission for this year`
-- 2027-28, still eligible: 30% of $1 200 = $360, under the $403 cap.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2027 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1200 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `the remission, in dollars, is` 360
-- 2027-28 after moving out before 1 July 2027: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2027 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1200 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `no remission for this year`
-- Applied 1 December 2024 (2024-25), asked about 2024-25 with no CPI figures: 30% of $1 500 = $450, capped at $379.41.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2024 (YMD 2024 12 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1500 TRUE EMPTY EQUALS `the remission, in dollars, is` 379.41
-- Applied 1 December 2024 (2024-25); asked about 2023-24 under s 4(1D): its maximum is not deposited.
#ASSERT `How much is remitted on my rates this year` 2023 (YMD 2024 12 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1500 TRUE `illustrative Hobart CPI` EQUALS `not covered by the deposited law` `the financial year begins before 1 July 2024: the maximum remission for it is set by regulations that are not deposited (the 2024 Regulations start from 2024-25)`

§§ `Council rates -- the surviving spouse`

#ASSERT `Can I apply for the rates remission as the surviving spouse` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may apply, and the remission can cover only the year you apply in and, if your late spouse was eligible and living there on its 1 July, the year before`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for the rates remission as the surviving spouse` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the conditions of s 4(4) are not met`
#ASSERT `Is my late spouse's unpaid remission given to me` 2025 2026 2026 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my late spouse's unpaid remission given to me` 2028 2026 2028 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my late spouse's unpaid remission given to me` 2029 2026 2028 TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Council rates -- telling the council, penalties, repayment`

#ASSERT `By what day must I tell my council` (YMD 2026 11 15) EQUALS YMD 2027 6 30
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell my council` (YMD 2027 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2027 6 30
#ASSERT `By what day must I tell my council` (YMD 2027 7 2) EQUALS YMD 2028 6 30
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined over my rates remission` EQUALS 2

-- Not living in the property on 1 July 2026, yet given the 2026-27 remission: the Commissioner may require repayment.
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner make me repay my rates remission` 2026 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Commissioner make me repay my rates remission` 2026 (YMD 2026 8 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `How long do I have to object and then apply for review` EQUALS `Review periods` WITH `days after the repayment notice to lodge a written objection` IS 60, `days after the decision on the objection to apply to the Magistrates Court` IS 60
